1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,900
Barcelona lost a Champions League semi-final… because they weren’t watching a corner.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,700
May 7, 2019. Anfield.

3
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:13,950
Liverpool had lost the first leg 3–0.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,850
And Mohamed Salah and Roberto Firmino were both missing.

5
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,950
Divock Origi scored after 7 minutes.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,700
Then, early in the second half, Georginio Wijnaldum scored twice in 2 minutes.

7
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,300
3–3 on aggregate.

8
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:30,700
79 minutes. Liverpool win a corner.

9
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:34,900
Trent Alexander-Arnold puts the ball down… and starts to walk away.

10
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:38,400
Barcelona’s players turn their backs. They’re still getting organised.

11
00:00:38,450 --> 00:00:41,400
Then he spins round and whips it in.

12
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:45,900
Origi is unmarked… and fires it in first time. 4–0.

13
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:49,800
Liverpool were in the final. Less than 4 weeks later, they won it.

14
00:00:49,850 --> 00:00:53,080
Would you have spotted it? Tell me in the comments.
